en.description:
A cryptocurrency transaction consists of n coins, each with a serial number. A valid serial number satisfies:
1. Its length is 10 to 12 characters;
2. The first 3 characters are distinct uppercase English letters;
3. The next 4 characters give the minting year, which must be between 1900 and 2019 (inclusive);
4. The following characters give the denomination, which must be one of 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 500, 1000;
5. The character right after the denomination is the last character of the serial number; the serial number must end with exactly one uppercase English letter.

A 1% fee is deducted from the total of this transaction, and no fractions are allowed, so the result is rounded down. Find the integer obtained after deducting the fee from the sum of the denominations of all valid coins.
